        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Menindee Lakes, Menindee, Menindee County, New South Wales, Australia\n- Organizations: Central Darling Shire\n- Natural features: Darling River\n\nFacts:\n- Menindee is a small town in the far west of New South Wales, Australia.\n- Menindee is in Central Darling Shire and on the banks of the Darling River.\n- Menindee is frequently but erroneously spelled \"Menindie\".\n- The sign-posted population of Menindee is 980.\n- The 2011 census population of Menindee was 449.\n- Menindee Lakes lie in the far west region of New South Wales, Australia, near the town of Menindee.\n- Menindee Lakes are located in Menindee County.",
